Mike for NativeCluster, version @VERSION@, built @DATE@

This is a modified version of Mike, the open-source legal AI platform by
Open Legal Products (https://github.com/open-legal-products/mike), changed
to run as an app on NativeCluster (https://www.nativecluster.com): each
person's copy runs on their own computer, keeps their documents there, and
sends every model call to their group's own Macs. It is based on upstream
commit 3422ab5ffd91f9b679e3644b59ed3a24fb707ac3 (2026-11-23); every change is
in the source below, under nativecluster/ and in the commits after that one.

Mike and this modified version are licensed under the GNU Affero General
Public License, version 3 (the file LICENSE beside this one), with no
warranty. The complete corresponding source of this package is at
https://github.com/pablothe/mikeos, commit @COMMIT@.

Other software in this package keeps its own licence:
- Node.js: runtime/LICENSE
- PostgREST, GoTrue (Supabase Auth), and PostgreSQL's libpq with the
  libraries it uses: stack/notices
- the backend's, the web pages' and the launcher's npm packages: each
  package's own licence file, in its node_modules folder
- the bundled contract templates: their publishers' licences and notices,
  kept in the files (docs/preset-templates.md in the source)
